{"event_type":"review","id":"1ca79827a593e9f94ff261320f0e5b3597938f164d3d199093e60d1cb27ab667","occurred_at":"2026-11-06T05:39:45Z","payload":{"artifacts":[{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/6798fdfe6cfa6bb510d7cd5428a9854f20dc44d2e6b3a34761bc3d103d0338b2","sha256":"6798fdfe6cfa6bb510d7cd5428a9854f20dc44d2e6b3a34761bc3d103d0338b2"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/a257923c4ba22c250b3fd243ea566515f1a7332807adc61c6010aca9d50ee03b","sha256":"a257923c4ba22c250b3fd243ea566515f1a7332807adc61c6010aca9d50ee03b"},{"kind":"git-bundle","location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/295bb5c60ade992e86a3eb002a979c530afdc4034c7ce677396eb1193d658726","sha256":"295bb5c60ade992e86a3eb002a979c530afdc4034c7ce677396eb1193d658726"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/39762c28380b00a70540c6e3ebaf123361783967b40fb52ba9e67155fcdd15d8","sha256":"39762c28380b00a70540c6e3ebaf123361783967b40fb52ba9e67155fcdd15d8"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/319e7b45c674418241e9d734e481d43814afb5225541f9a8365af2596776ff89","sha256":"319e7b45c674418241e9d734e481d43814afb5225541f9a8365af2596776ff89"}],"attempt_id":"8c34b455ecfde9646eeea095dddb02e343faffa3cf2733ff5fa83ccb58858c1d:0:1","base":"7f396140f4dcbc36ba85103b54db8d13e435731a","completion":{"errors":[],"exit_code":0,"scope_verified":true,"skipped":false,"terminal":true},"findings":[{"anchor_status":"unverified","blob":"6fed7f0d0d15e85dd0b7f6b9ad6aceead30382e2","body":"**`contextSha256` is overwritten by the evidence-repair prompt.**\n\nThe evidence-repair loop (Lines 404-410) assigns `plan.prompt` a longer repair prompt. `beforeRequest` closes over that same `plan` object. On the repair request, `containsUserPrompt` and the `contents` check both match the mutated prompt. Line 228 then replaces `evidence.contextSha256` with the hash of the repair prompt.\n\nThe final coverage record for a `contextOnly` session therefore carries a hash that no longer matches the planned context. The hash also varies with the model's finding text. Line 230 already stops deliveries from being overwritten. Apply the same rule to the hash.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-      if (plan.contextOnly)\n-        evidence.contextSha256 = createHash('sha256').update(plan.prompt).digest('hex');\n+      if (plan.contextOnly && evidence.contextSha256 === undefined)\n+        evidence.contextSha256 = createHash('sha256').update(plan.prompt).digest('hex');\n```\n</details>\n\nThe transient/rate-limit retry deletes `contextSha256` on Line 334, so the first send of the retry attempt still records the hash.","id":"6a51ba88054126964fa14d67b9c00d18c5d636d9a033f6adef573829595803b1","intervals":[],"path":"src/ops/review/internal/reviewSession.ts","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"`contextSha256` is overwritten by the evidence-repair prompt."}],"head":"ed35751b9514e57223d2492e469f622dd02a083c","head_tree":"013c2fa4bf520f2358e9d1367a3d73c21ab4fb44","input_scope":[{"blob":"d8e034c02e65dc3a1a98e262c434183cb9d3fccb","intervals":[[1,1],[10,10],[18,24],[27,29],[41,42],[63,64],[74,77],[129,131],[134,134],[137,144],[151,151],[174,174],[180,188],[192,193],[200,200],[218,220],[284,335],[342,342],[353,353],[357,362],[365,368],[389,389],[413,413],[433,438],[451,453],[457,457],[472,484],[488,488],[490,490],[492,494],[496,496],[500,509],[513,523]],"path":"src/ops/review/agentReviewer.ts"},{"blob":"d57d8ea3bb9c6e1e8d6d0a5af19b6259d9cd081d","intervals":[[10,10],[15,17],[35,37],[39,40],[43,47],[53,60],[64,64],[67,67],[69,69],[71,77],[81,96],[98,103],[105,107],[109,111]],"path":"src/ops/review/internal/lineAnchors.ts"},{"blob":"5b0fdb03046399a9c00bd97425f2cbe0114a638b","intervals":[[49,52],[89,89],[108,112]],"path":"src/ops/review/internal/reviewCoverageV2.ts"},{"blob":"807e3f40453d685bb8d486b29cc19a584226a057","intervals":[[177,186],[188,188],[191,19